linux-rockchip64-ysp-sgguard (6.18.40+rk3588av1fwport20260725sgguard1-0ubuntu1~rk1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Diagnostic-only kernel. Do not install this as a system kernel; it exists
    to attribute the GRD/RKMPP system-heap scatterlist corruption that oopses
    the production kernel 3/3 on the first RDP login.
  * Identical to the production forward-port source
    6.18.40+rk3588av1fwport20260725 — same Armbian 6.18.40 worktree, same
    contiguous 0001-0075 vendor series, same production config (MPP
    service/RKVENC2/RKVDEC2/AV1DEC enabled, RGA as a module, KASAN and lockdep
    disabled) — plus one temporary commit: the system-heap scatterlist
    page_link guard from kernel-drivers/patches/system-heap-sg-guard/.
  * The guard snapshots every dma-buf attachment's page_link array and
    re-compares it at attach, post-map, begin/end CPU access, pre-unmap, detach
    and release. It reports the owning device and the before/after value, and
    skips a corrupted sync instead of faulting, so the machine survives and
    keeps logging. Runtime knobs: system_heap.sg_guard (default on) and
    system_heap.sg_guard_panic.
  * Built through the PPA so Launchpad's gcc 15.2/binutils 2.46 compiles it,
    matching the production kernel's toolchain. Local Armbian builds use gcc
    13.3, which left the earlier KASAN comparison unable to separate "KASAN
    masks it" from "the gcc-13 build lacks it".
  * Co-installable with the production kernel: separate source and binary
    package names, so installing it neither replaces nor upgrades
    linux-image-ysp-rockchip64. Select it with kernel-revert.sh.
  * Drop this package once the writer is identified.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 21:30:00 -0700
